# "Target opponent exiles a card from their hand. If this spell was cast from a graveyard, draw a card": the draw does not
# depend on the exile. Bot2 plays out its whole hand on turn 2 (everything but the Swamp costs {0}) after exiling Mox
# Emerald from the hand-cast Negotiation on turn 1, so the flashback on turn 3 finds an empty hand: Bot2 is asked
# nothing (`! Bot2.Choose`) and Bot1 still draws (hand: 2 + the turn-3 draw - the Swamp played + the flashback draw = 3).

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Ruthless Negotiation
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
10 Swamp

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Ornithopter
Lotus Petal
Mox Sapphire
10 Swamp

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ruthless Negotiation.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot2.Choose(Mox Emerald)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Lotus Petal.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Graveyard.Ruthless Negotiation.Cast(Bot2; Ability: Flashback)
! Bot2.Choose

[Expect]
Exile = Mox Emerald; Ruthless Negotiation
Bot2.Hand.Count = 0
Bot1.Hand.Count = 3
